    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d223-a10-a1">

                <pb facs="0657" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg443"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Pollock to Lord
                        Lyons</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-11-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 23, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> I have the honor to recall to your
                    excellency’s attention that there still remain here about one hundred of Her
                    Majesty’s subjects very unwilling prisoners, and to earnestly solicit an early
                    intercession on their behalf.</p>
                <p>My personal dread of having to spend Christmas (usually a season of happy family
                    reunion) in this desolate city, decides me to write also to influential friends
                    in the House to lay our unfortunate case before Lord Granville.</p>
                <p>Trusting that your lordship’s firm representation will suffice to change the
                    present capricious decision of the authorities,</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>POLLOCK.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
